@page "/about"

<PageTitle>About - Loper Family Tree Builder</PageTitle>

<div class="page-header">
    <div>
        <h1>About Loper Family Tree Builder</h1>
        <p>Local-first family-history archive and genealogy research system with secure hosted-deployment readiness.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="dashboard-grid">
    <section class="page-card">
        <h2>Installed Version</h2>
        <div class="summary-value">1.0.13</div>
        <p>Production Release Baseline</p>
    </section>

    <section class="page-card">
        <h2>Preservation Policy</h2>
        <p>Robert J. Loper Legacy Numbers are historical data. They are preserved exactly and are not automatically renumbered, normalized, recalculated, replaced, or reformatted.</p>
    </section>
</div>

<section class="page-card">
    <h2>Release Focus</h2>
    <p>Version 1.0.13 consolidates the cumulative feature set into a production-release baseline with local archive validation, recovery checks, hosted-deployment readiness, release health reporting, and installer integrity verification.</p>
</section>

<section class="page-card">
    <h2>Release Boundaries</h2>
    <p>Production hosting and Authenticode signing require external provider and verified-publisher credentials. The software does not silently select a hosting vendor or embed signing credentials.</p>
</section>
